[ ] Mini-C

    [X] Add support for typedefs while parsing
        ...so, just push/pop "namespaces" as we parse {...} (i.e. the
        compound_statement rule), populate current namespace when we
        encounter a typedef, and add a callback to the parser for the
        TYPE_NAME pseudo-toktype

    [X] Attempting to parse any of the following results in RecursionError:
            int x(int);
            ((void *)0)

    [X] When evaluated, typedefs should be persisted somewhere
        [-] More generally, we should figure out the 4 namespaces:
            https://www.spinellis.gr/cscout/doc/name.html
            * Tags for a struct/union/enum
            * Members of struct/union (actually a separate namespace is assigned to each struct/union)
            * Labels
            * Ordinary identifiers (termed objects in the C standard)
            ...see also: notes/namespaces.txt

            ===> NEVER MIND?.. I think we're going to keep MiniC super
            dynamic, like basically the semantics will just be Python's,
            but we'll implement some Python classes representing pointers,
            structs/unions, etc.
            But e.g. the structs/unions are going to dynamically add keys
            to themselves whenever you refer to them. Like Python's
            types.SimpleNamespace.
            So... we're not gonna actually pay any attention to struct/union
            definitions.

    [X] Attempting to parse these returns None:
            int x = (int)y;
            (void) sizeof x;
            sizeof x;

    [X] We're not parsing pointer derefrences correctly:

        >>> mini.parse('return p;', 'statement').pprint()
        return: jump_statement
          ident: p

        >>> mini.parse('return *p;', 'statement').pprint()
        multiplicative_expression
          ident: return
          *
          ident: p

    [X] Handle references correctly (e.g. `x += 1`, `&x`)
        See: on_assign__assignment_expression, the '+=' case
        See: MiniC.on_unary_expression, the '&' case

    [ ] Handle postfix increment/decrement correctly?!..
        Omg. How is the semantics even defined, and can we do that within our
